    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (78.64) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.46) headlining the lineup as the clear objective choices. Both benefit immensely from the high-upside matchup against V\u00e1squez (xERA 4.75), an arm providing the largest SP skill advantage of the day (+18%). While **Trea Turner** is locked into the #2 hole for a boost in counting stats, **Kyle Schwarber**\u2019s leadoff placement (+10%) maximizes his exposure to that favorable matchup, cementing him as an elite play despite the standard platoon neutralizer. **Yordan Alvarez** (74.26) remains a set-and-forget anchor, whose elite xwOBA of .454 effectively renders the opponent's xERA irrelevant.\n\nOur most critical bench decision involved **Casey Schmitt**, who fell just short of the 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" with a 38.76 score. While he enjoyed a batting order benefit (+10%), the combination of a tough matchup against Harrison (xERA 3.41) and a significant negative platoon split (-11%) effectively muted his ceiling. Conversely, **Dillon Dingler** (56.21) and **Junior Caminero** (63.30) secured their spots, the former buoyed by an opportunistic dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and the latter by his high-leverage spot in the order. \n\nWe are monitoring two primary risks: the back-to-back challenges posed by Gilbert (xERA 3.22) and McDonald (xERA 2.97). These elite arms significantly suppress the projections for **Carson Benge** and **Christian Yelich**, forcing them toward the bottom of our starters. Additionally, **Luke Raley** faces a specific situational headwind; while his platoon advantage is positive, he is staring down a high-end catcher pop time (1.89s) and a pitcher who excels at holding runners, significantly capping his stolen base potential in a category we prioritize above all else. Proceed with caution on these fringe starts as we aim to preserve our remaining game caps.",
